{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383698-mechanics-of-animal-companions","id":1383698,"title":"Mechanics of Animal Companions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-24T18:04:21-07:00","id":1383698,"title":"Mechanics of Animal Companions","content":"I am building a book-standard (not a thin-blood) vampire, with no additional xp.<br /> <br /> I plan to build a fairly standard high-clan vampire, with high social skills. This is not necessarily Camarilla, and indeed might be a classy Anarch. Basic concept is a Ventrue or Toreador who is a complete bastard, but loves, loves, loves animals. The pc will breed pedigree dogs and train them as &quot;animal minions&quot;. I know this is easier to build as VtR Ventrue or V20 Old Clan Tzimisce, due to clan discipline spread, but it's in a canon V5 environment.<br /> <br /> The upshot is, I want a character who dotes on their <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MisterMuffykins\" target=\"_blank\">pretty doggies</a>, but quickly switches into &quot;<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RightHandAttackDog\" target=\"_blank\">Release the hounds!</a>&quot; mode. If it matters, I am planning on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samoyed_(dog)\" target=\"_blank\">Samoyeds</a>.<br /> <br /> What is the best (read: mechanically efficient) way to build animal companions?<br /> <br /> Here are the options I see so far:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Obvious Discipline</b></u> Take Predator Type Cleaver for Animalism 1 (Bond Famulus). This gives me a single animal, no special communication advantage beyond &quot;sit&quot; and &quot;stay&quot; type commands, and it will defend itself and me. There's some synergy with higher levels of Animalism, though the dog breeder thing isn't central to the concept and I am not likely to take higher levels. If I did it would be Sense the Beast, anyway. Control rolls are based on Charisma+Animal Ken, which is unusual for a discipline, but fits my build nicely.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Long-Shot Disciplines</u></b> I have read and re-read the sections on Dominate and Presence in V5. I am unable to find where the RAW rules forbid using these disciplines on animals.<br /> <br /> Dominate makes mention of it in neither the general description of the discipline, nor the description of Compel. (I would mainly use Compel for the &quot;sit&quot;, &quot;stay&quot;, and &quot;attack&quot; type commands.) It refers to &quot;living beings&quot;, &quot;mortals&quot;, and &quot;victims&quot;, but not &quot;humans&quot;.<br /> <br /> Presence does, here and there, use the term &quot;people&quot;, but in neither the general description, nor in the description of Awe. Otherwise, it uses &quot;onlooker&quot;, &quot;victim&quot;, &quot;mortal&quot;, etc.<br /> <br /> Yes, yes, I get it. Nearly 30 years of common usage doesn't apply these disciplines to animals. In a canon V5 environment, however, where is it written? And, yep, it's rules-lawyering, but is it worth a shot?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Backgrounds</u></b> Take high levels of Charisma and Manipulation (standard for a high clan), and high levels of Animal Ken. Then buy the dogs mechanically as Allies, Retainers, or even Mawla. I figure as Retainers or Allies they would be the equivalent of Weak Mortals, giving me up to five or ten dogs eventually. I am guessing the usual pool to interact with them would be Charisma + Animal Ken, so same as Bond Famulus, but a great deal cheaper.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Loresheet</u></b> Take the Loresheet Theo Bell 1 (Rebel Cell) defining the 3 dot group of Allies as the dog pack. I know it's a stretch using this for animals, but if I use the pack to track down and tear apart Camarilla ghouls, maybe?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Ghouling</u></b> What it says on the tin. Feed a dog blood, then command it. Except, with a limited number of ghouls, it seems wasteful.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> So, what do you think? Bond Famulus seems next to worthless as a stand-alone power. Should I pitch the other options? Do you have any other mechanical work-arounds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T19:16:15-07:00","id":1383707,"title":"","content":"If you had picked Cavaliers, I would have had the perfect picture for you. It's not super-professional... just something I slapped together in like four minutes with some photoshop.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimages.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/59sznn3p/cavaliers.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","user":"Legendre","date":". 04-24-2020, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T14:28:59-07:00","id":1383845,"title":"","content":"That image is a hundred kinds of awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T22:42:15-07:00","id":1384361,"title":"","content":"Why thank you! I had sort of imagined it as a high-class Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T02:47:28-07:00","id":1384388,"title":"","content":"I designed Lord Kelvin as a vampire who continued to experiment with science after he embrace. <br /> <br /> Made him responsible for the hounds of Baskerville and other legends (his escaped experiments), etc.<br /> <br /> I found a plethora of combo disciplines to augment ghouls and animal ghouls specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}